---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import TimestampDiff from '../../components/TimestampDiff.jsx';
---
<ToolLayout title="Timestamp Difference Calculator" description="Calculate the exact difference between two dates/times in days, hours, minutes, and seconds.">
  <TimestampDiff client:load slot="tool" />

  <h2>Why manual date math is error-prone</h2>
  <p>Calculating the exact difference between two dates by hand — especially across month boundaries, leap years, or different timezones — invites arithmetic mistakes that a direct calculation avoids entirely.</p>

  <h2>How to use this calculator</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Enter a start date/time and an end date/time.</li>
    <li>See the exact difference in days, hours, minutes, and seconds.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Common mistakes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Not accounting for timezone differences</strong> between the two timestamps being compared, if they originate from different sources.</li>
    <li><strong>Manually counting days across month boundaries</strong>, which is easy to get wrong given varying month lengths and leap years.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Use cases</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Calculating exact duration between two events for reporting or logging</li>
    <li>Checking how much time remains until a deadline or expiry</li>
    <li>Debugging a time-based calculation by verifying the expected difference</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>FAQ</h2>
  <p><strong>Does this account for timezone differences automatically?</strong> Calculations use the timestamps as entered — ensure both are in the same timezone reference (or explicitly convert first) for an accurate difference.</p>
</ToolLayout>
